{{ToonInfo|Toon=Tisha|extra=Tissue Box|Date=July 12, 2024|with={{CI|Flutter|name=true}}, {{CI|Shelly|name=true}}, and {{CI|Teagan|name=true}}|Pronoun=She}}

==Appearance==
Tisha is a light cyan anthropomorphic tissue box. She has three freckles on each cheek and between her eyes, and two eyelashes on both her upper and lower lids. A white tissue comes out the top of her head, and a smaller one is fastened on her neck, resembling a jabot. Her dress is a dark blue bell-shape, with a rounded, light blue trim.

In her Info Card and ability animation, she wields a small wooden {{TI|Feather Duster|name=true}} with a black handle and deep brown feathers with light brown edges. When hurt by a [[Twisted]], she has a somewhat worried look on her face.  

==Personality==
Tisha is a chipper [[Toon]] who is obsessed with cleaning, and dislikes mess. She overworks and stresses herself, as implied in her interactions with {{CI|Astro|name=true}}, {{CI|Razzle & Dazzle|name=true}}, and {{CI|Cosmo|name=true}}. Despite this, she refuses an offer of help from {{CI|Cocoa|name=true}}. Other Toons often ask her to clean or organize for them, which she can enjoy—but she can also get quite frustrated with, and even refuse, repetitive cleaning requests, seen in her interaction with {{CI|Sprout|name=true}} and Astro. She wishes the other Toons were tidier and didn't create as much work for her, often asking or begging them to be more mindful. She can be hostile towards those who don't appreciate what she does, like  {{CI|Vee|name=true}}. She also likes to be punctual.

She speaks politely in most cases and values some level of etiquette. When not upset, she tries to avoid causing any issues, changing the subject or reassuring others, if something she says causes certain reactions. She acts a bit more blunt or accusatory when she’s frustrated or stressed, but it isn’t a common occurrence, sometimes apologizing.

Her relationship with {{CI|Brusha|name=true}} is complicated and strained, and she can be seen ignoring her. Shortly after [[Gardenview]] shut down, she had a falling out with Brusha, accusing her of pretending to be friends when they're not, despite it not being entirely her fault, and expressing that their friendship only existed because of the [[Show]], and that they didn't have to follow the show's rules anymore. She still cares about Brusha, and shows extreme guilt for scarring her emotionally, unable to get past her own irritation and hurt from the event. It seems to be a common behavior of her to give the silent treatment when upset, as she also does it towards Vee, likely to avoid snapping again at worst.

