==[[Toon of the Week]] Quests==
{{TOTWQuests|Clean 3 Ichor Puddles with Tisha's "Tidy Up!" [[Ability]].|Restore 300 Stamina with the {{TI|Feather Duster|name=true}} [[Trinket]].|Encounter {{CI|Twisted Tisha|name=true}} 5 times.}}

===Rewards===
*1 Quest completed: {{AT|Tisha Fan}} [[Title]]
*2 Quests completed: {{SI|Golden Tisha!|name=true}} [[Sticker]]
*3 Quests completed: {{Skin|Golden Tissues|toon=Tisha}} [[Skin]]

===Strategies===
*For the first Quest, use Tisha and play until you either encounter an [[Ichor Leak]] or {{CI|Twisted Finn|name=true}}, then use her [[Ability]] as much as possible near Ichor Puddles. It’s recommended to use {{TI|Sweet Charm|name=true}} and/or {{TI|Ghost Snakes In A Can|name=true}}, as well as picking the {{CDI|Practice|name=true}} and/or {{CDI|Rehearsal|name=true}} [[Cards]] to reduce the 50 second cooldown.
*For the second Quest, play as Pebble or Coal with {{TI|Feather Duster|name=true}}, pick up all Items you see or find, also try to run to use up your Stamina, to allow the [[Trinket]] to regenerate. {{CI|Cocoa|name=true}}, {{CI|Yatta|name=true}}, and {{CI|Gigi|name=true}} all have Abilities that spawn Items, allowing for more opportunities to get Stamina. The best Toon however would be {{CI|Bassie|name=true}} if you have her, as she can simply use her Ability to spam drop and pick up Items, quickly refilling her Stamina after running.
*For the third Quest, it is recommended to just play normally, as {{Type|Common}} [[Twisteds]] like her are still fairly common on the early Floors. However, when you reach a high Floor like 25, it is recommended to restart, as Commons get rarer the farther you go. If there's a distractor (and you aren't one), ask them to bring [[Twisted Tisha]] to the [[Elevator]] during [[Panic Mode]] so you can encounter her.

==Requirement Strategies==
*For the first and only requirement, focus on picking up [[Research Capsules]] and extracting [[Machines]]. The Machine and Capsule count increases the further you descend, so you can earn more {{II|Ichor|name=true}}.

==Strategies==
Tisha is a great all-rounder due to her versatile Stats, with high [[Skill Check]], [[Movement Speed]], and a good support [[Ability]]. This means she is easily able to switch between supporting other Toons, extracting, and helping or being the primary distractor. Her 4{{Star}} Skill Check allows her to complete [[Machines]] at the average rate despite her 2 Star [[Extraction Speed]], and her 4 Star Movement Speed can nearly negate her 2 Star [[Stamina]] when used strategically.

Tisha's Active Ability, {{AI|Tisha|name=true}}, can support Toons that need a speed boost. Some ways this Ability can be used include:
*Boosting a Toon that is close to getting hit by a [[Twisted]];
*Boosting a Toon who is out of Stamina (though this would require good communication, as she can't see if a Toon is low on Stamina, unlike {{CI|Astro|name=true}});
*Using '''Tidy Up!''' at the start to support other Toons in finding Machines/Twisteds (especially viable, as the radius is about as big as the [[Elevator]]);
*Supporting a Toon in getting to the Elevator during [[Panic Mode]];
*Boosting a Distractor to help them distract more easily, especially if they are dealing with the {{Debuff|Slow|}} [[Debuff]];
*Boosting a Toon who is extracting on Treadmill Machine.

Be aware of '''Tidy Up!'''<nowiki/>'s pulse radius, as it can be difficult to land the boost if Tisha is too far away from her targets—but, depending on the teammate's [[Stealth]], she shouldn't get too close, either, or risk taking a hit herself. If multiple Toons could use an assist but are too far apart to fit in her pulse radius, prioritize boosting lower mobility Toons over ones with higher mobility, as Toons with low Movement Speed and Stamina will need it the most.

To boost a distractor, land her pulse and make a quick getaway. She should be able to boost them with little to no issues if her Distractor has 1-2 Star Stealth (granted they don't cut a sharp corner), but if they have 3 Star Stealth, keep a bit of distance. If they are looping around an island or near an object, Tisha can hide behind the obstruction and then boost them, as her pulse works through barriers. This same tactic can be applied with Distractors that have more than 3 Star Stealth, but be more cautious. If possible, she can also stand behind a wall they pass close to and sweep when they're in range; this is a safer but more difficult method.

Another core part of Tisha's Ability is the fact it can clean/remove certain Debuff sources. [[Ichor Leaks]] are less of a problem when she's on the team, as her Ability will clean up Ichor Puddles within her radius. She could prioritize puddles in a path to Machines, in a route to the Elevator during Panic Mode, or in a distractor's preferred distraction area, though less Ichor Puddles on the Floor is beneficial no matter what. The best time to do this is when also boosting a Toon to make use of the Ability, especially with how Ichor Puddles (from Ichor Leaks) reappear after some time and her long cooldown making boosting others hard. These strategies can also be applied when {{CI|Twisted Finn|name=true}}, who spawns permanently cleanable Ichor Puddles, is on the Floor; she also has the ability to force {{CI|Twisted Barnaby|name=true}} out of puddles. If {{CI|Twisted Tisha|name=true}} is on the same Floor as an Ichor Leak or Twisted Finn, Tisha can clean up any Ichor Puddles that are increased in size from her Twisted Counterpart's ability, reducing the threat and danger. {{CI|Twisted Brusha|name=true}}'s graffiti can also be removed from Machines, removing any sort of hindrance towards extraction (especially for Skill Check focused Toons or those with certain Trinkets); this isn't always necessary, though it can be somewhat helpful as long as the current circumstances don't prompt saving the speed boost for later.

If there's multiple Tishas, you could split up the tasks, in order to ensure there's always at least one who can provide a potentially lifesaving speed boost, while another can focus on cleaning when needed.

Tisha is a great early Toon for garnering large amounts of [[Ichor]]. Her speed can allow her to more easily survive on higher Floors as well as encounter most Twisteds safely; her extraction is decent enough (especially with Trinkets like {{TI|Magnifying Glass|name=true}} or {{TI|Participation Award|name=true}}) which allows her to complete a good amount of Machines fairly quickly; her Active Ability will give her an extra +5 Ichor per Floor if it's used. Within teams, her speed boost can keep teammates alive, therefore making it more efficient and easy to reach higher Floors, resulting in larger rewards of Ichor.

Overall, she is a good starter Toon who can help make Ichor Leaks less of a problem. Even without supporting, she can do just fine in a solo run, cleaning Ichor Puddles for her own benefit, and having good all-round Stats. Getting her early on is a good idea if you intend on grinding Ichor more quickly.

